.TH tublock n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tublock
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBblock\-beta\fR diagram into a \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR model (best\-effort), so it can render natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine — no browser. It is one of the graph\-type parsers the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade dispatches to; you normally call \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR rather than this module directly.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tublock 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tublock::parse text      ;# -> tudiagram model dict
.CE
.PP
The result is a \fBtudiagram\fR model and is rendered with \fBtclutils::tudiagram::toSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR (or via the \fBtuflow\fR facade).
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
a b c            -> three boxes (bare ids on one line)
a["Text"]        -> box
a("Text")        -> rounded
a(("Text"))      -> circle
a{"Text"}        -> diamond
a{{"Text"}}      -> hexagon
a(["Text"])      -> stadium
a[("Text")]      -> cylinder
a --> b          -> edge with arrowhead
a --- b          -> edge without arrowhead
a -->|label| b   -> edge with a label
a -- label --> b -> edge with a label
block:groupId ... end  -> flattened (inner blocks kept, group box not drawn)
columns N        -> ignored (layout hint)
space / space:N  -> ignored (empty grid cell)
style/classDef/class/click -> ignored
.CE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tublock
package require tclutils::tudiagram

set src {block-beta
    columns 3
    a["Frontend"] b["API"] c["DB"]
    a --> b
    b --> c
}
set m [::tclutils::tublock::parse $src]
::tclutils::tudiagram::writePng $m block.png -scale 3
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
v1 limitations (honest): the grid geometry of block\-beta (columns, widths, \fB:N\fR spans, explicit placement) is NOT reproduced — \fBtudiagram\fR lays the blocks out as a top\-down graph. Group boundaries are flattened. Node shapes map to \fBtudiagram\fR \fBbox\fR/\fBrounded\fR/\fBcircle\fR/\fBdiamond\fR/\fBhexagon\fR/\fBstadium\fR/ \fBcylinder\fR (subroutine \fB[[..]]\fR \-> \fBbox\fR). Edge endpoints not declared as blocks are created on first use.
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (renderer), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUBLOCK <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no blocks found).
